          "unit_id": "numbers_colors",
          "title": "Unpacking",
          "description": "Objetos y colores: a/an, plurales, this/that/these/those y el lugar del adjetivo. Y el posesivo 's: my grandma's lamp.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "colors_intro",
              "title": "a/an, plurals, this/that",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Unpacking",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "Knock, knock! Is this a good time?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Yes, come in!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "These are for you. Two towels and a lamp."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Oh, thank you! Is that an old lamp?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "Yes, it's my grandma's lamp. It's a bit ugly!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "No, it's a nice green lamp."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "And what are those?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "These? They're photos of my family. And this is a fan, a Spanish fan for hot days."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "Hot days? In Bristol? Ha! You need an umbrella, not a fan!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Is that an umbrella?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Sam",
                        "text": "Yes. It's a big black umbrella. And it's for you!"
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "Lucía's room is small, but it's nice. Her suitcase is open on the bed. There's a knock at the door."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "articles_demonstratives",
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"These are for you.\" We use these for…",
                        "options": [
                          "one thing near",
                          "many things near",
                          "many things far"
                        ],
                        "answer": 1
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Is that an old lamp?\" Why an and not a?",
                        "options": [
                          "old starts with a vowel sound",
                          "lamp is plural",
                          "it's a question"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"a nice green lamp\": in English, adjectives go…",
                        "options": [
                          "before the noun",
                          "after the noun"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "explanation": "El adjetivo va antes: «a green lamp»."
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Two towels\": the plural adds…",
                        "options": [
                          "-s",
                          "-es",
                          "nothing"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "articles_demonstratives",
                    "title": "a/an, plurals and this/that/these/those",
                    "explanation": "«A» y «an» significan un, una. Usamos «a» antes de sonido de consonante y «an» antes de sonido de vocal:\n- «a lamp», «a big umbrella»\n- «an umbrella», «an old lamp»\n\nEl plural se forma normalmente con «-s» («towels») y con «-es» después de s, sh, ch o x («boxes»). Hay irregulares: «person» → «people», «child» → «children».\n\n«This» (este, esta) y «these» (estos, estas) indican cerca; «that» (ese, aquel) y «those» (esos, aquellos), lejos.\n\nEl adjetivo va antes del nombre y no cambia en plural (nunca «a lamp green» ni «greens lamps»):\n- «a green lamp», «two green lamps»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Cerca",
                        "Lejos"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Singular",
                          "this lamp",
                          "that lamp"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Plural",
                          "these towels",
                          "those photos"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "This is a fan.",
                      "These are photos of my family.",
                      "Is that an umbrella?",
                      "It's a big black umbrella."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "possessive_s",
                    "title": "Possessive 's",
                    "explanation": "Para decir de quién es algo, en inglés se pone el dueño delante con «'s»:\n- «my grandma's lamp» (la lámpara de mi abuela)\n- «Sam's guitar» (la guitarra de Sam)\n\nSi el dueño es un plural acabado en «-s», solo se añade el apóstrofo: «my parents' house» (la casa de mis padres). Con los plurales irregulares se usa «'s»: «the children's room».\n\nPara preguntar de quién es algo:\n- «Whose umbrella is this? — It's Sam's.»\n\nOjo: no confundas el posesivo con la contracción de «is»: «Sam's a musician» (= «Sam is») / «Sam's band» (la banda de Sam).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Dueño",
                        "Posesivo",
                        "En español"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Sam",
                          "Sam's guitar",
                          "la guitarra de Sam"
                        ],
                        [
                          "my grandma",
                          "my grandma's lamp",
                          "la lámpara de mi abuela"
                        ],
                        [
                          "my parents",
                          "my parents' house",
                          "la casa de mis padres"
                        ],
                        [
                          "the children",
                          "the children's room",
                          "la habitación de los niños"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "It's my grandma's lamp.",
                      "Priya's family is in Leicester.",
                      "Whose umbrella is this? — It's Sam's.",
                      "My parents' house is in Valencia."
                    ]
                  }
                },
